"text": "You ask the universe why. Why this job? Why this loss? Why any of it? And the universe says nothing. Albert Camus called that silence the absurd. We want meaning and the world doesn't answer. Most people do one of two things. They pretend there's an answer or they give up. Camus said there's a third way. Keep living fully knowing there's no answer. Like a man pushing a rock up a hill forever, who decides the climb is his. You don't need the universe to approve of your life. You just need to live it. What would you do tomorrow if you stopped waiting for a sign? Follow for sourced philosophy.",
